Oh, please. Do you really believe that the least shred of uncertainty in 
a matter renders you utterly incapable of decision and action with regard 
to that matter? I dispute this. In fact, people (including yourself) act 
decisively with regard to matters about which they are uncertain, and it 
happens *all the time*.

> Eric again: <Which beliefs do you hold to be indisputable and beyond doubt?  But
